results.abstract:
This Per- and Polyfluoroalkyl Substances (PFAS) Site Assessment Progress Report was prepared by AECOM Technical Services, Inc. for the National Aeronautics and Space Administration (NASA) under Contract 80KSC019D0010, Task Order 80KSC021F0096. The purpose of this report is to document 2024-2025 assessment activities at the South Repeater Building, Solid Waste Management Unit (SWMU) 121.

A site assessment for PFAS began in July 2023 following confirmation of perfluorooctanesulfonic acid (PFOS) in groundwater above the then-current Environmental Protection Agency and Florida Department of Environmental Protection screening levels.  The objectives of the 2024-2025 PFAS assessment activities were to:
• Continue to assess the extent of PFAS affected environmental media in the South Repeater Building area;
• Identify locations for groundwater and surface water sampling;
• Qualitatively and quantitatively characterize the potential migration of PFAS to environmental media (groundwater and surface water).

Results of the PFAS assessment activities indicated PFAS detections in groundwater and surface water were above current screening criteria, with the highest concentrations within the vicinity of the South Repeater Building and the western boundary of the Site within the wooded area. Results of the groundwater investigations indicate that groundwater has not been horizontally delineated throughout the Site. Results indicate that vertical delineation has been completed excluding two areas, one to the north of the South Repeater Building and one approximately 700 to 800 feet west of Tel-4 Road on the southern boundary. PFAS has not migrated downward to the 54 to 59-foot depth interval, excluding these two areas. Delineation efforts are ongoing, and an Interim Measure for groundwater containment and treatment has been implemented.
